# Git and GitHub Identity

- Every commit must use author and committer identity
  `da03 <dengyuntian@gmail.com>`.
- Verify the effective identity before committing. Use per-command Git
  configuration or environment variables if a repository override would use
  another identity.
- Never use `Cursor Agent`, `cursoragent`, or another AI identity as author,
  committer, or co-author.
- Never add Cursor attribution or AI co-author trailers to commit messages.
- Use only GitHub account `da03` for pushes, pull requests, and other GitHub
  writes. If authentication resolves to another account, stop and ask the user.
